{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "eval.2026-07-28-eval-184200.rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "title": "RAG Ingestion, Retrieval & Grounded Answers",
  "description": "# Retrieval-augmented generation: ingestion to grounded answers\n\nReads left to right across the serving path: source imports and ACLs are normalized, hash-classified, chunked with versioned metadata, embedded, and published only when vector, fragment, and keyword stores agree on one version. Queries are rewritten into parallel vector and keyword searches, fused and reranked, permission-filtered, then either produce a cited answer from strong evidence or an explicit “I don’t know.”\n\nDashed exception paths isolate unparseable content, retry transient embedding failures, dead-letter exhausted work, and rebuild a new embedding generation in the background before atomic promotion or rollback. Feedback and coverage gaps inform future ingestion priorities.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
